rlm-gh-repo-init [--public|--private] [OWNER/REPO]

Create a GitHub repository from the current directory and push,
provided no remote is configured yet.

The argument must be in OWNER/REPO form (e.g. ecerulm/my-project).

If no OWNER/REPO argument is provided, defaults to
<github-username>/<current-dir> (username looked up via 'gh api user')
and prompts for confirmation before continuing.

Visibility is set by --public or --private. If neither flag is given,
prompts for visibility (private/public), defaulting to private on a
bare Enter.

Requires: gh, git.
